WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.538
- I've had one panic attack in my life,

00:00:01.538 --> 00:00:02.371
- Okay.

00:00:02.371 --> 00:00:03.700
- And I read this on you
like, that you suffer

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.160
from panic attacks and anxiety, right?

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:05.993
Yes.

00:00:05.993 --> 00:00:07.657
- I had one when I was
pregnant with my little girl

00:00:07.657 --> 00:00:08.490
- You were pregnant!

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.610
- And I was driving and I couldn't move.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.190
Like, I was like, oh my
God, am I about to die?

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.023
And I was literally

00:00:13.023 --> 00:00:13.856
looking at my hands and
That's what it feels like.

00:00:13.856 --> 00:00:15.100
I was like, and I couldn't breathe,

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.190
like it was shallow breathing,

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:17.330
- Yes!
I'd never experienced that

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.490
and it was my first
pregnancy that that happened

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:20.323
with my little girl.

00:00:20.323 --> 00:00:22.690
And I read that you suffer from anxiety

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.010
and panic attacks, too.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:24.843
I do, I do.

00:00:24.843 --> 00:00:26.430
- And, how do you deal with that?

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.040
I have had them my whole life,

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.050
it's so interesting for me and
this is obviously, probably

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.660
with you too but I don't get
them when I'm performing.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.050
Like, I feel most at home
Yeah.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:34.883
when I'm on stage,

00:00:34.883 --> 00:00:36.300
like I don't have any anxiety about that

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.480
but I get them just in my day-to-day life

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.440
and you know my life changed overnight

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.280
with, Two Broke Girls.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.550
I you know, went from being a nanny, ahh,

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:44.620
and a bartender full-time

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.330
and then was on national
television, a lot of pressure,

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.520
as you know.
Yeah.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.353
American Idol!
Cocktail waitress.

00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:50.186
It happened to you too!

00:00:50.186 --> 00:00:51.019
I was a cocktail waitress!
Yeah.

00:00:51.019 --> 00:00:51.852
To national TV.

00:00:51.852 --> 00:00:52.930
We have so much in common Beth
We are so...

00:00:53.798 --> 00:00:55.798
I can't wait to ride horses in the woods

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:57.583
and have like,

00:00:57.583 --> 00:00:58.850
the other,
I'll be on a four-wheeler

00:00:58.850 --> 00:00:59.870
and you stay on your horse.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:00.703
Okay!

00:01:00.703 --> 00:01:01.620
(laughing)
That sounds good!

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.453
Yeah, your horse, your mare

00:01:02.453 --> 00:01:03.810
We'll keep her away from us,
I'm like my butt hurts!

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:04.827
Beth, ahh.
I don't want

00:01:04.827 --> 00:01:06.410
(laughing)
her to learn bad behavior.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:10.430
Anyways so, I started to notice
that my anxiety got worse.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:11.500
Not while I was performing,

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.430
just off-camera red carpets.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.263
I don't do well,
Yeah.

00:01:14.263 --> 00:01:16.200
with anything like that.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.460
And so,
Red carpets are horrible!

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.293
They're the worst!

00:01:18.293 --> 00:01:19.550
Yeah.
People don't know but it's,

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:20.736
Your smile,
Yes!

00:01:20.736 --> 00:01:21.934
- all of a sudden I start
looking like I have a disease.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.197
And it goes like this
Cuz it starts twitching.

00:01:23.197 --> 00:01:24.030
Yes!

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.340
And I'm like, then I have
to make myself laugh,

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:26.173
so I'm like,

00:01:26.173 --> 00:01:27.006
ha ha ha ha ha
- Oh my God.

00:01:27.006 --> 00:01:28.609
(laughing)
I try to get it to like not.

00:01:28.609 --> 00:01:29.755
They're like, Kelly, Kelly!

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:30.588
You're like,
Yeah.

00:01:30.588 --> 00:01:31.952
am I hearing voices, or
is someone talking to me?

00:01:31.952 --> 00:01:32.785
I don't know what's happening?

00:01:32.785 --> 00:01:33.618
- And they're yelling at you.

00:01:33.618 --> 00:01:34.619
Yeah.
It's not polite.

00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:36.260
It's like, KELLY!

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.941
And I'm like you know.

00:01:37.941 --> 00:01:39.484
And then they get you
Yeah.

00:01:39.484 --> 00:01:40.635
in the one angle
And then they get

00:01:40.635 --> 00:01:41.468
you looking terrible
you looking really hot.

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:42.301
Yeah.
Yeah.

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:44.200
It's
I can see how that would cause

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.370
a panic attack.
But all of it, you know.

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:47.730
And actually, Whitney
Cummings who's co-creator

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:50.170
of Two Broke Girls and I said to her,

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.350
you know when, my character on the show

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.610
had a horse living in New
York City, named Chestnut.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:57.420
And when the horse was on
the show I noticed that

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.260
I was calmer, more grounded at rehearsal,

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.915
I was so happy I mean
I always loved animals.

00:02:01.915 --> 00:02:02.748
Yeah.

00:02:02.748 --> 00:02:03.581
But there was something about the horse,

00:02:03.581 --> 00:02:04.880
and I mentioned it to Whitney,

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.220
and Whitney was like, I have a friend,

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.100
her name is Cassandra Ogier,

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.712
she's this incredible equine therapist.

00:02:09.712 --> 00:02:10.545
Oh yeah.

00:02:10.545 --> 00:02:11.850
You don't have to ride, you
don't have to do anything

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.880
it's all on the ground,
it's super spiritual.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.640
Go, work with her.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.610
And she completely changed my life.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:18.770
Wow!

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:21.030
'Cause horses are prey animals,

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.980
so they only live in the present moment.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.210
You know they can smell if
a mountain lion is far away.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.380
So, in order to work with them,

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.920
which you know, but if
you're not a horse person

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:30.980
people don't understand this,

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:35.160
but they will only respond
to your authentic behavior

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:35.993
in that moment.

00:02:35.993 --> 00:02:38.650
So, if you're scared but
you're trying to show that

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:39.960
you're not scared, they're gonna' be like,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:40.793
boy, bye.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:41.840
Like because,
They sense it.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:42.673
They sense it.

00:02:42.673 --> 00:02:43.506
Yeah.

00:02:43.506 --> 00:02:45.430
And so, something I
found really empowering,

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:46.730
which is why I believe in equine therapy,

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.760
is that when you realize this huge animal,

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.190
that could kill you, responds when

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:53.070
you're just your pure authentic self.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.970
Whether you're happy, sad, angry,

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:55.880
whatever it is that day,

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.150
you get to show up as
you are and that's enough

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.980
and their gonna' want to
respond and communicate

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.180
because,
Wow.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.460
They're feeling your authentic truth

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:03.840
and I thought that, that was

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:04.840
one of the most empowering things

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.560
and it really helped me
get over my panic attacks.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:07.813
That's really cool!

